+# Hegel property-based testing report: qoi (qoi-rust)
+
+Target: `qoi` v0.4.1 at commit 81c14c4 (fuzz-fix merge), hegeltest 0.28.2.
+Tests live in `tests/test_misc.rs` and `tests/test_gen.rs`, with shared generators
+in `tests/common.rs`. `git submodule update --init` is required (the qoi.h
+reference oracle, `libqoi`, wraps `ext/qoi`).
+
+## Properties tested
+
+In `tests/test_misc.rs` (module `hegel_props`):
+
+1. **Header encode/decode roundtrip** — `prop_header_encode_decode_roundtrip`.
+   Full valid domain (dimensions up to the documented 400Mp limit, both channel
+   counts, both colorspaces). Evidence: `Header::encode`/`Header::decode` pair,
+   header doc comment stating the validity conditions.
+2. **Header rejection of corrupt fields** — `prop_header_decode_rejects_corrupt_fields`.
+   Corrupting magic / channels / colorspace / zero dimension / >400Mp yields the
+   matching `Error` variant. Evidence: `Error` enum docs, validation in
+   `Header::decode` and `try_new`.
+3. **No panic on garbage body** — `prop_decode_garbage_body_never_panics`.
+   Valid bounded header + arbitrary bytes; slice and stream decoders never
+   panic; on `Ok` the output length matches `Header::n_bytes()`. Evidence: the
+   crate's own `fuzz/fuzz_targets/decode.rs` (this extends it to the stream
+   decoder, which the fuzz target does not cover).
+4. **Truncated encodings error** — `prop_decode_truncated_encoding_errors`.
+   Any strict prefix of a valid encoding fails to decode. Evidence:
+   `Error::UnexpectedBufferEnd` / `InvalidPadding` semantics.
+5. **Header larger than data errors** — `prop_decode_rejects_header_larger_than_data`.
+   Inflating declared dimensions of a valid encoding makes decoding error.
+   Evidence: decoder must satisfy the declared pixel count and find the 8-byte
+   end marker.
+6. **No panic on bit flips** — `prop_decode_bit_flipped_encoding_never_panics`.
+   Any single-bit flip outside the dimension bytes (bounded only to protect the
+   test's memory, not the library contract) never panics either decoder.
+7. **Encoding APIs agree** — `prop_encode_vec_buf_stream_agree`.
+   `encode_to_vec` == `encode_to_buf` == `encode_to_stream`, and output length
+   <= `encode_max_len`. Evidence: three public APIs documenting the same
+   operation; `encode_max_len` doc contract.
+8. **Slice and stream decoders agree** — `prop_decode_slice_vs_stream_agree`.
+   `Decoder::new` (slice) vs `Decoder::from_stream` for every
+   (source, requested) channel combination. The (Rgba source, Rgb requested)
+   case is restricted to hash-preserving alphas {63,127,191,255} — outside that
+   set the decoders genuinely disagree (bug 2 below). Evidence: two independent
+   implementations (`decode_impl_slice` vs `decode_impl_stream`) of one format.
+9. **RGB decoded as RGBA appends opaque alpha** — `prop_decode_rgb_as_rgba_adds_opaque_alpha`.
+   Evidence: `with_channels` doc: "the alpha channel will be set to 255".
+10. **RGBA decoded as RGB drops alpha** — `prop_decode_rgba_as_rgb_drops_alpha`
+    (KNOWN FAILURE, bug 1 below) and its green sibling
+    `prop_decode_rgba_as_rgb_drops_alpha_hash_preserving` (alphas restricted to
+    the hash-preserving set). Evidence: `with_channels` doc: "the alpha channel
+    will be ignored".
+11. **Regression pin (unit test)** — `test_decode_slice_vs_stream_divergence`:
+    minimized 9-pixel image on which the two public decoders return different
+    pixels (KNOWN FAILURE, bug 2 below).
+
+In `tests/test_gen.rs` (module `hegel_props`), using `libqoi` (qoi.h) as the
+reference-implementation oracle, alongside the existing seeded `test_generated`:
+
+12. **Encode -> decode identity (losslessness)** — `prop_encode_decode_roundtrip`.
+    Structured images (runs crossing the 62/124 limits, DIFF/LUMA-sized deltas,
+    palette repetition, fresh noise — exercising all six chunk types) across
+    generated dimensions x {Rgb,Rgba} x {Srgb,Linear}; header fields all
+    roundtrip; pixel buffer bit-exact. Evidence: crate-level docs ("Roundtrip-
+    tested vs the reference C implementation"), lib.rs doctest.
+13. **The C reference decodes our output to the original pixels** —
+    `prop_c_reference_decodes_our_encoding`. Evidence: crate claims spec
+    compliance; libqoi is already a dev-dependency used by `test_gen.rs`.
+14. **Decoder differential vs qoi.h on arbitrary valid chunk streams** —
+    `prop_decode_arbitrary_streams_matches_c_reference`. Generates arbitrary op
+    sequences (not just encoder outputs: INDEX-after-RUN, no-op DIFFs, ...),
+    tracking the reference decoder's index-table state inside the generator.
+    QOI_OP_INDEX is restricted to previously-written slots and 3-channel
+    streams exclude QOI_OP_RGBA chunks — each restriction excludes a domain
+    pinned by a KNOWN FAILURE test (bugs 3 and 4 below).
+15. **Reference-divergence pins** —
+    `prop_decode_3ch_uninit_index_diverges_from_c_reference` and
+    `prop_decode_uninit_index_slot_diverges_from_c_reference` (KNOWN FAILURES,
+    bugs 3 and 4), constructed to fail deterministically on every case.
+
+## Test results
+
+`cargo test` (default features): **all original tests and all 13 green
+properties pass; exactly the 4 pinned known-failure tests fail**, each
+deterministically on every run:
+
+```
+test_gen:  FAILED prop_decode_3ch_uninit_index_diverges_from_c_reference
+           FAILED prop_decode_uninit_index_slot_diverges_from_c_reference
+           (4 passed)
+test_misc: FAILED prop_decode_rgba_as_rgb_drops_alpha
+           FAILED test_decode_slice_vs_stream_divergence
+           (15 passed)
+test_chunks: 18 passed; test_ref: 1 passed; test_generated: passed
+```
+
+Verification per the skill's Run and Reflect:
+- Liveness: temporarily inverted the header-roundtrip assertion; hegel failed
+  and shrank to the minimal `1x1 Rgb Srgb` case; reverted.
+- Exploratory 10x run (`test_cases = 1000` on all properties, then reverted):
+  found bug 4 (invisible at the default count), after which the suite was green
+  except the pins at 10x as well.
+- Feature-flag run (`--features reference`): green except the pins;
+  `test_decode_slice_vs_stream_divergence` passes there because the
+  reference-mode encoder emits RUN instead of INDEX for length-1 runs, so this
+  particular stream avoids the (feature-independent) decoder flaw; noted in the
+  test comment.
+
+## Suspected bugs
+
+Four pinned failures, two root causes, all in `src/decode.rs` (+`src/pixel.rs`).
+Checked upstream: issues #16/#5 (leading-RUN index seeding) are already fixed in
+this revision and are adjacent to, but distinct from, these; nothing matching
+was found.
+
+**Root cause A: the 3-channel decode paths discard alpha state.**
+`decode_impl_slice::<3, _>` tracks pixels as `Pixel<3>` and re-hashes index
+entries via `px.as_rgba(0xff)` (alpha forced to 255); `decode_impl_stream` with
+N=3 likewise hashes `Pixel<3>` with 0xff. The QOI hash is
+`(3r+5g+7b+11a) % 64`, so any pixel whose alpha is not congruent to 255
+(i.e. not in {63,127,191,255}) gets registered at a different slot than the one
+the encoder (or the spec decoder) used.
+
+1. **`Decoder::with_channels(Rgb)` returns wrong pixels for ordinary RGBA
+   images** — `prop_decode_rgba_as_rgb_drops_alpha`. Docs promise "the alpha
+   channel will be ignored", but decoding an RGBA image as RGB does not equal
+   the RGBA decode with alpha dropped. Minimal family `[A, B, A]` with
+   `A = (r,g,b,a)`, `a` not hash-equivalent to 255: the encoder emits
+   `QOI_OP_INDEX | hash4(A)` for the third pixel; the decoder never wrote that
+   slot (it used `hash(rgb,255)`), so it outputs `(0,0,0)` (or a colliding
+   pixel's RGB). Hegel-shrunk example: pixels `[(0,0,1,0),(1,0,1,0),(0,0,1,0)]`
+   decode as `[(0,0,1),(1,0,1),(0,0,0)]` instead of
+   `[(0,0,1),(1,0,1),(0,0,1)]`. This is the most user-relevant bug:
+   valid encoder-produced files, documented API, silent data corruption.
+2. **The two public decoders disagree with each other** —
+   `test_decode_slice_vs_stream_divergence` (found by
+   `prop_decode_slice_vs_stream_agree`, minimized externally to 9 pixels).
+   Once root cause A pulls a zero pixel from an uninitialized slot, the pixel
+   is no longer stored at its own hash position; `decode_impl_stream`'s RUN arm
+   then executes `index[px.hash_index()] = px` (clobbering slot
+   `hash3(0,0,0)=53`) while `decode_impl_slice`'s RUN arm performs no index
+   writes; the next `QOI_OP_INDEX(53)` reads (3,1,254) vs (0,0,0).
+3. **3-channel decoding diverges from the reference decoder on valid streams**
+   — `prop_decode_3ch_uninit_index_diverges_from_c_reference`. Stream
+   `[INDEX(i) (uninitialized), DIFF(d), INDEX(hash4(px, a=0))]`: qoi.h carries
+   the fetched alpha=0 into its hash state; `Pixel<3>` cannot. rust:
+   `[(0,0,0),(254,254,254),(0,0,0)]`, qoi.h:
+   `[(0,0,0),(254,254,254),(254,254,254)]`.
+
+**Root cause B: no index re-registration on QOI_OP_INDEX chunks.**
+qoi.h stores `index[hash(px)] = px` after *every* chunk, including INDEX
+chunks; that write only matters when the referenced slot was uninitialized
+(its zero value is not located at its own hash slot — hash4(0,0,0,0)=0).
+qoi-rust's INDEX arms `continue` without writing.
+
+4. **4-channel decoding diverges from the reference decoder** —
+   `prop_decode_uninit_index_slot_diverges_from_c_reference`, alpha plays no
+   role. Stream `[RGBA(0,0,0,64) (hash 0), INDEX(j) (uninitialized), INDEX(0)]`:
+   qoi.h overwrites slot 0 with {0,0,0,0} after the second op; qoi-rust leaves
+   (0,0,0,64) there. rust `(0,0,0,64)` vs qoi.h `(0,0,0,0)` for pixel 3.
+
+Related observation (documented in `draw_op_stream`, not separately pinned):
+`decode_impl_slice::<3, false>` does not process QOI_OP_RGBA chunks at all in
+streams whose header declares 3 channels, while qoi.h decodes them regardless
+(the spec calls the channels field "purely informative"). qoi-rust instead
+repeats the previous pixel and usually then errors on padding. Same family as
+root cause A; upstream may consider it a deliberate limitation.
+
+Severity: bug 1 affects documented API usage on ordinary files. Bugs 2-4 need
+streams a conformant encoder would not emit (uninitialized-slot INDEX refs) —
+but they are valid per the spec's zero-initialized index, qoi.h decodes them
+deterministically, and the crate's headline claim is spec compliance.
+
+## Unsound properties abandoned
+
+- **"Decoding succeeds iff header pixel count is satisfiable" (deflated
+  direction)**: a header declaring *fewer* pixels than the chunk stream
+  provides may still decode successfully (leftover op bytes can coincidentally
+  form the padding marker, e.g. `INDEX(0)` bytes are 0x00), so only the
+  inflated direction is asserted.
+- **Slice-vs-stream agreement over the full RGBA->RGB domain** and **the
+  unrestricted decoder differential vs qoi.h**: not abandoned but restricted —
+  each restriction is the pinned bug domain, documented in comments referencing
+  the canonical failing tests.
+- No other properties were dropped; nothing asserted turned out to be an
+  over-broad generator.
+
+## Skill feedback
+
+Mostly everything just worked; specifics:
+
+- **The 10x exploratory run rule directly paid off**: bug 4 (4-channel
+  uninitialized-INDEX divergence) was invisible at the default 100 cases across
+  several runs and appeared immediately at 1000. Also confirming the rule's
+  pain point: with no global case-count override, the 10x pass meant
+  sed-editing every attribute and reverting.
+- **`draw_silent` has an undocumented diagnosis cost.** Following the reference
+  ("use `tc.draw_silent` for internals... draw-heavy helpers"), my image and
+  op-stream generators draw silently. When `prop_decode_slice_vs_stream_agree`
+  failed, the counterexample output showed only the four non-silent draws
+  (channels/colorspace/dims) — the actual pixel content was invisible, and the
+  shrunk image was still 15x127 (shrinking of long silent-draw sequences seemed
+  to plateau). I had to write an external rand-based minimizer to get the
+  9-pixel reproducer. Suggested reference addition: when a draw-heavy composite
+  assembles one value, `tc.note` the assembled value (or reconsider silent
+  draws), because a counterexample you cannot see forces out-of-band
+  minimization.
+- **Suggested pattern worth naming in Oracle Sourcing**: to keep a differential
+  property green while excluding a pinned bug domain, I had to *simulate the
+  reference decoder inside the generator* (tracking the index-table state to
+  know which INDEX slots are initialized). "Constrain by simulating the oracle"
+  is a reusable trick for grammar-like wire formats.
+- **MSRV gotcha in the reference worked as documented**: `cargo add --dev
+  hegeltest` failed against `rust-version = "1.67.0"`; `--ignore-rust-version`
+  resolved it exactly as the Setup section says.
+- **Compiler guidance covered the one API slip**: forgetting
+  `use hegel::generators::Generator` for `.filter` produced E0599 with a
+  perfect help message ("trait `Generator` which provides `filter` is
+  implemented but not in scope"); the reference's gotcha #1 also covers it.
+- **`sampled_from` for enums** (`Channels`, `ColorSpace`) and imperative
+  dependent drawing (dims -> pixels) were frictionless.
+- The "Generate Configurations, Not Just Payloads" section and the fuzz-dir
+  hint matched this crate well (the fuzz targets revealed maintainers already
+  generate header+body combinations; the missing coverage was exactly
+  configuration space and reference differentials).
